  "notes": [
    "Keys (A, s_i), y and the decoys are derived from SHAKE-256(seed, nonce) rather than NumPy's RNG; signatures verify with this C verifier and match Python's serialized size, but are not byte-identical to Python's.",
    "Only the REGULAR (embed=None) and ATTRIBUTABLE FPE (embed='fpe') modes are implemented.",
    "Link tags and FPE extraction (feistel_inv) are implemented; Merkle roots, salt/ae modes and constant-time serialization remain Python-only.",
    "mu = (32-byte payload << 128) | first 16 bytes of HMAC-SHA256(dk_mac, payload); the MAC is computed in Python and passed as 48 bytes."
  ],
  "kernel_selftest": true,
  "merkle_selftest": true,
  "all_pass": true
